{
  "id": "longest-palindromic-subsequence",
  "questionId": "longest-palindromic-subsequence",
  "slug": "longest-palindromic-subsequence",
  "title": "Longest Palindromic Subsequence",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "strings",
    "palindrome"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "a palindrome is symmetric - if you fix the leftmost and rightmost characters of a substring, when can they both be part of the palindromic subsequence?",
    "define dp[i][j] as the length of the longest palindromic subsequence within s[i..j] (inclusive)",
    "if s[i] == s[j] (and i != j), those two characters bookend a palindrome, so dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]",
    "if s[i] != s[j], the best you can do is drop one end or the other: dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])",
    "base case: dp[i][i] = 1 for every single character; fill the table by increasing substring length, and the answer is dp[0][n-1]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "filling the table in the wrong order - dp[i][j] depends on dp[i+1][j-1], dp[i+1][j], and dp[i][j-1], all of which need shorter substrings computed first",
    "forgetting the i == j base case of 1 for single characters",
    "confusing this with longest palindromic substring, which requires contiguous characters and has a different recurrence"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a string `s`. Unlike a substring, a subsequence does not\nneed to use consecutive characters, it just needs to preserve their\nrelative order.\n\n**Find the length of the longest subsequence of `s` that reads the same\nforwards and backwards.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= s.length <= 1000",
      "s consists of lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a string of length 1 (always a palindrome of length 1)",
      "the whole string is already a palindrome",
      "a string with no repeated characters (answer is 1)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
